hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3410","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: (No), rather you should show him hospitality."
"3411","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came to us. We presented them with fresh dates to eat and offered them water. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These are among the blessings about which you will be questioned."
"3412","I said to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), ""I saw such-and-such a person who makes supplication and mentions goodness; he mentions that you (peace be upon him) gave him two dinars."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""But as for so-and-so, I gave him such and such (an amount), but he neither praised nor spoke any good."
"3413","the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Whoever some good was done to him, and he says: 'May Allah reward you in goodness' then he has done the most that he can of praise."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2035)"
"3414","I saw such and such person expressing gratitude, he mentioned that you (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave him two dinars. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That person, I had given him between ten and one hundred, but he did not thank me nor did he mention it. No person leaves from me with something for his need, which he carries under his arm, except that it is only fire from Hell. Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! Why do you give to such people? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They keep asking me, and Allah the Exalted does not approve of my being stingy."
"3415","I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say, ""Whoever good is done to, and he only expresses gratitude by praising (the doer), then he has shown thankfulness. And whoever conceals it, he is ungrateful. And whoever adorns himself with something false to appear (as such), he is like one who wears two garments of falsehood."
"3416","I Myself will give its reward. Fasting is a shield; so whoever is fasting should not use foul language or act ignorantly. If someone abuses him or hurts him, he should say: I am fasting, I am fasting."
"3417","“Whoever fasts one day in the cause of Allah, Allah will keep the Fire away from his face the distance of seventy autumns (years) for that day.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1717)"
"3418","""I heard the Messenger of Allah say"" 'Whoever spends on a pair of things in the cause of Allah, he will be called from the gates of Paradise: O slave of Allah, this is good for you. Paradise had (several) gates. Whoever is one of the people of Salah, he will be called from the gate of prayer. Whoever is one of the people of Jihad, will be called from the gate of Jihad. Whoever is one of the people of charity will be called from the gate of charity. And whoever is one of the people of fasting will be called from the gate of Ar-Rayyan."" Abu Bakr said: ""Is there any need for anyone to be called from all of these gates? Will anyone be called from all of them, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""Yes, and I hope that you will be among them."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2439)"
"3419","""Whoever spends on a pair (of things) in the cause of Allah, the Mighty and Sublime, he will be called in Paradise: 'O slave of Allah, here is prosperity, Whoever is one of the people of Salah, he will be called from the gate of salah. Whoever is on of the people of charity, he will be called from the gate of Ar-Rayyan.' Abu Bakr As-Siddiq said: 'O Messenger of Allah, no distress or need will befall the one who is called from those gates. Will there be anyone who will be called from all these gates?' The Messenger of Allah said: 'Yes, and I hope that you will be one of them.""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2238)"
"3420","In Paradise there is a gate which is called Rayyan through which only the people who fast would enter on the Day on Resurrection. None else would enter along with them. It would be proclaimed: Where are the people who fast that they should be admitted into it? And when the last of them would enter, it would be closed and no one would enter it. (Using translation from Muslim 1152)"
"3421","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “There is a gate in Paradise called ‘Rayyan’. It has been prepared for those who fast. When the last of them enters through it, it will be closed.”"
"3422","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""(Allah said), 'Every good deed of Adam's son is for him except fasting; it is for Me. and I shall reward (the fasting person) for it.' Verily, the smell of the mouth of a fasting person is better to Allah than the smell of musk."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 5927)"
"3423","""The Prophet said: 'Allah, may He be blessed and exalted, says: Fasting is for me I shall reward for it. The fasting person has two moments of joy: When he breaks his fast and when he meets his Lord. By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the smell that comes from the mouth of the fasting person is better before Allah than the fragrance of musk."" ' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2213)"
"3424","The fasting person will have two joys: one joy at the time of breaking his fast, and one joy when he meets his Lord. The smell from the mouth of the fasting person, which comes due to leaving food, is purer with Allah than the fragrance of musk."
"3425","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) prepared an army. I presented myself before him and said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace"
"3426","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said,"
"3427","narrates: These are the hadiths that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, narrated before us. Then he narrated some hadiths among which it was also mentioned that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Fasting is a shield."
"3428","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The supplication of three people is not rejected: the fasting person until he breaks his fast, the just ruler, and the supplication of the oppressed."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): The narrator named Abu al-Mudillah is Ubaydullah bin Abdullah; he was a resident of Madinah and is trustworthy."
"3429","narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him: ""Whoever provides iftar to a fasting person, he will receive a reward like that of the fasting person, and there will be no decrease in the reward of the fasting person."
"3430","I am fasting. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: As long as food is being eaten in the presence of a fasting person, the angels continue to pray for mercy for that fasting person."
"3431","The Prophet ﷺ as saying: The two months of 'Id (festival), Ramadan and Dhu al-Hijjah, are not defective. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2323)"
"3432","“The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ‘Whoever fasts Ramadan and spends its nights in prayer, out of faith and in hope of reward, his previous sins will be forgiven.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1326)"
"3433","narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever fasts in Ramadan, safeguards its limits, and protects what should be protected, then his past sins are forgiven."
"3434","'When Ramadan begins, the gates of Paradise are opened, the gates of Hell are closed, and the devils are chained up."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2099)"
"3435","“When the first night of Ramadan comes, the satans and mischievous jinns are chained up, and the gates of the Fire are closed, and none of its gates are opened. The gates of Paradise are opened and none of its gates are closed. And a caller cries out: ‘O seeker of good, proceed, O seeker of evil, stop.’ And Allah has necks (people) whom He frees (from the Fire), and that happens every day.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1642)"
"3436","narrates: When the last ten days of Ramadan would arrive, the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would wake his wives as well, and he (peace be upon him) would gird himself with determination and spend the entire night in worship."
"3437","'A'isha (Allah be pleased with her) reported that when the last ten nights began Messenger of Allah ﷺ kept awake at night (for prayer and devotion), wakened his family, and prepared himself to observe prayer (with more vigour). (Using translation from Muslim 1174)"
"3438","A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, what if I were to testify that there is no god except Allah and you are the Messenger of Allah, and I were to perform the five Ṣalawāt (obligatory ritual prayers), pay the Zakāh (obligatory charity), fast ˹the month of˺ Ramaḍān and stand ˹for night ṣalāh˺ in it, then whom I would be among? He (the Prophet ﷺ) said, ""From the Truthful ones and the Martyrs."""
"3439","The Prophet ﷺ said: One of you should not say: I fasted the whole of Ramadan, and I prayed during the night in the whole of Ramadan. I do not know whether he disliked the purification; or he (the narrator) said: He must have slept a little and taken rest. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2415)"
"3440","The Prophet ﷺ was the most generous person, and he used to become more so (generous) particularly in the month of Ramadan because Gabriel used to meet him every night of the month of Ramadan till it elapsed. Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite the Qur'an for him. When Gabriel met him, he used to become more generous than the fast wind in doing good. (Using translation from Bukhārī 4997)"
"3441",""" I heard the messenger of Allah say: 'When you see the crescent then fast, and when you see it, then stop fasting, and if it is obscured from you (too cloudy), then work it out (fro the beginning of the month, to complete thirty days)""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2120)"
"3442",": ""The Messenger of Allah said: 'Fast when you see it and stop fasting when you see it, and if it is obscured from you (too cloudy), then count it as thirty (days).'"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2118)"
"3443","""When you see the crescent then fast, and when you crescent then fast, and when you see it, stop fasting. If it is obscured from you (too cloudy), then fast thirty days."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2119)"
"3444","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to count the days in Sha'ban in a manner he did not count any other month; then he fasted when he sighted the new moon of Ramadan; but if the weather was cloudy he counted thirty days and then fasted. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2325)"
"3445","""Do not fast until you see the crescent, and do not stop fasting until you see it, and if it is obscured from you (too cloudy), then work it out."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2121)"
"3446","""A Bedouin come to the Prophet and said; 'I have sighted the crescent tonight.' He said: 'Do you bear witness that there is none worthy of worship except Allah, and that Messenger?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'O Bilal, announce to the people that they should fast tomorrow. ""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2113)"
"3447","The people looked for the moon, so I informed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that I had sighted it. He fasted and commanded the people to fast. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2342)"
"3448","Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The two months of Eid are not reduced—Ramadan and Dhu al-Hijjah. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): This narration can have two meanings. One of them is: The two months of Eid are in reality not reduced, even though according to our sight they may appear to be less. This happens when there is dust or clouds or something similar that prevents us from sighting the moo"
"3449","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him): \""A month (sometimes) consists of twenty-nine (29) days.\"""""
"3450","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) asked: How many days are left for the month (to end)? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) meant the month of Ramadan. We replied: Twenty-two (22) days have passed and eight days are left. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Twenty-two (22) days have passed and seven days are left; seek it in tonight. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The month is like this and like this. He said this three times, twice indicating ten and once indicating nine."
"3451","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “(Sometimes) the month is of thirty days and (sometimes) the month is of twenty-nine days. If clouds cover you, then complete the count of thirty.”"
"3452","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) separated himself from his wives for a month. On the morning of the twenty-ninth day, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came, so one of those present said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! It has only been twenty-nine days. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: A month can also be of twenty-nine days. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) indicated three times with all the fingers of both hands, and on the third time, he indicated with nine fingers (i.e., a month can also be of twenty-nine days)."
"3453","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""A month can also be of twenty-nine days."
"3454","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""The month is like this and this,"" (at the same time he showed the fingers of both his hands thrice) and left out one thumb on the third time. (Using translation from Bukhārī 1908)"
"3455","I folded one finger (meaning that sometimes the month is of twenty-nine days as well)."
"3456","narrates: His uncles testified before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that they had sighted the new moon of the first (of Shawwal), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the people to go out the next day to perform the Eid prayer."
"3457","""the Messenger of Allah said: 'Fast when you see it and stop fasting when you see it, and if it is obscured from you (too cloudy), then count it as thirty (days). ""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2117)"
"3458","""Do not anticipate the month until you see the crescent before it, or you complete the number of days. Then fast until you see the new moon, or you complete the number of days."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2126)"
"3459","""the Messenger of Allah said: 'Fast when you see it and stop fasting when you see it, and if it is obscured from you (too cloudy), then count it as thirty (days). ""' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2117)"
"3460","""It was the custom among the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ, that if any of them was fasting and the food was presented but he had slept before eating, he would not eat that night, nor the following day until the evening. Qais bin Sirmah Al-Ansari fasted and came to his wife at the time of Iftar, and said to her: 'No, but I will go and bring something for you.' He worked during the day, so his eyes (sleep) overcame him. Then his wife came, and when she saw him she said: 'You shall be disappointed.' About the middle of the next day he fainted. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, so this Ayah was revealed: 'It is made lawful for you to have sexual relations with your women on the night of the fasts. So they were very happy about that. 'And eat and drink until the white thread (light) of dawn appears distinct to you from the black thread (of night). (2:187)'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2968)"
"3461","""It was the custom among the Companions of Muhammad ﷺ, that if any of them was fasting and the food was presented but he had slept before eating, he would not eat that night, nor the following day until the evening. Qais bin Sirmah Al-Ansari fasted and came to his wife at the time of Iftar, and said to her: 'No, but I will go and bring something for you.' He worked during the day, so his eyes (sleep) overcame him. Then his wife came, and when she saw him she said: 'You shall be disappointed.' About the middle of the next day he fainted. That was mentioned to the Prophet ﷺ, so this Ayah was revealed: 'It is made lawful for you to have sexual relations with your women on the night of the fasts. So they were very happy about that. 'And eat and drink until the white thread (light) of dawn appears distinct to you from the black thread (of night). (2:187)'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2968)"
"3462","""When 'Until the white (light) thread of dawn appears distinct to you from the black thread (of night)' was revealed, the Prophet ﷺ said to me: 'That only refers to the whiteness of the day from the blackness of the night.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2970)"
"3463","When the verse ""Until the white thread of dawn appear to you distinct from its black thread"" was revealed, I took a white rope and a black rope, and placed them beneath my pillow ; and then I looked at them, byt they were not clear to me. So I mentioned it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He laughed and said: Your pillow is so broad and lengthy ; that is (i.e. means) night and day. The version of the narrator 'Uthman has: That is the blackness of night and whiteness of day. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2349)"
"3464","""The Messenger of Allah said to a man: 'Come to the blessed breakfast, - meaning Sahur."" ' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2165)"
"3465","""I heard the Messenger of Allah inviting people to have Sahur in Ramadan. He said: 'Come to the blessed breakfast."" (Hasan) Chatper 26. Calling Sahur ""Ghada"" (Breakfast) (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2163)"
"3466","“Eat Suhur, for in Suhur there is a blessing.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1692)"
"3467","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Allah and His angels bless those who are on the right flanks of the rows. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 676)"
"3468","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Bilal’s call to prayer should never prevent any one of you (the narrator is in d"
"3469","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates this statement of the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""Bilal gives the call to prayer during the night, so you may continue eating and drinking until Ibn Umm Maktum gives the call to prayer.\"" Ibn Shihab states: Ibn Umm Maktum was a blind man. He would not give the call to prayer until it was said to him: 'The true dawn has come, the true dawn has come.' (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): This"
"3470","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""Bilal gives the adhan at night (i.e., a little before true dawn), so you may continue eating and drinking until you hear the adhan of Ibn Umm Maktum.\"""""
"3471","""Bilal calls the Adhan during the night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls (the Adhan)"" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 637)"
"3472","""Bilal calls the Adhan at night to awaken those of you who are asleep, and so that those who are praying Qiyam cam return. Dawn is not when the light appears like this"" - and he gestured with his hand - ""rather dawn is when it appears like this: - and he gestured with his two forefingers. ' (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2170)"
"3473","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Ibn Umm Maktum gives the call to prayer at night (that is, a little before true dawn), so you may continue eating and drinking until Bilal gives the call to prayer."" Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) used to give the call to prayer when he saw the true dawn."
"3474","I may finish my suhoor first."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): These two narrations may confuse a person who does not have expertise in the science of hadith, and he may think that these two are contradictory, whereas this is not the case. This is because the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to alternate the duty of giving the adhan before true dawn (subh sadiq) between Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Ibn Umm Maktum (may Allah be pleased with him). On certain nights, Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) would give the adhan before true dawn so that the sleeping person would wake up and the one praying voluntary prayers would return (to eat suhoor). He would not give the adhan for the Fajr prayer. On those nights, Sayyiduna Ibn Umm Maktum (may Allah be pleased with him) would give the adhan for the morning prayer after the true dawn had occurred. And when it was Sayyiduna Ibn Umm Maktum's (may Allah be pleased with him) turn, he would sometimes give the adhan before true dawn, as we have mentioned earlier, and on those nights, Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) would give the adhan for the morning prayer after the true dawn had occurred. In this way, there remains no contradiction or difference between these two narrations."
"3475","The Prophet ﷺ as saying: How good is the believers meal of dates shortly before dawn. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2345)"
"3476","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Take suhoor, even if it is with a single sip of water."
"3477","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ as saying: The difference between our fasting and that of the people of the Book is eating shortly before dawn. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2343)"
"3478","""When this verse was revealed 'And as for those who can fast with difficulty, (e.g. an old man), they have (a choice either to fast or) to feed a miskin (poor person) (for every day). Those among us who did not want to fast would pay the fidyah, until the verse after it was revealed and abrogated this."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2316)"
"3479","I am fasting.'"" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): (The uncle of the narrator named Khalid bin Abdur Rahman) is Abdullah bin Mughira bin Abu Dhibab Dosi, and the narrator's name is Harith bin Abdur Rahman bin Mughira bin Abu Dhibab."
"3480","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""Whoever does not give up forged speech and evil actions, Allah is not in need of his leaving his food and drink (i.e. Allah will not accept his fasting.)"" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1903)"
"3481","narrates: He heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: ""There are many who perform voluntary prayers, but from their standing (in prayer at night) they gain nothing except staying awake (they do not receive any reward), and there are many who fast, but from their fasting they gain nothing except hunger (they do not receive any reward)."
"3482","“When anyone of you is fasting, let him not utter evil or ignorant speech. If anyone speaks to him in an ignorant manner, let him say: ‘I am fasting.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1691)"
"3483","I am fasting,' and if you are standing, then sit down."
"3484","The narrator states:) The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) forbade, through this, that the fasting person should respond to the one who insults him."
"3485","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the call to prayer is given for the prayer, that is, the Fajr prayer, and any one of you is in a state of major ritual impurity (janabah), then he should not fast that day."
"3486","I urge both of you that when you go to Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), inform him of this as well. Then both of them went to Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) and informed him of this, so he said: Those women have more knowledge. Sayyiduna Fadl bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) had informed me about this matter."
"3487","""Aishah and Umm Salamah, the wives of the Prophet informed me that the Prophet would find that it was Fajr while he was Junub from (relations with) his wives, then he would perform Ghusl and fast."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 779)"
"3488","I would see the water flowing between his shoulders, yet he would still observe the fast."
"3489","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would sometimes be in a state of janabah (major ritual impurity) at the time of true dawn during Ramadan, not due to a wet dream, yet he would still observe the fast."
"3490","I would see the water flowing down the skin and head of the Prophet (peace be upon him), and then I would also hear his recitation in the Fajr prayer, and he would be in a state of fasting. The narrator named Mutarrif states: I asked my teacher: Did this happen in Ramadan? He replied: The ruling is the same (whether it is Ramadan or outside of Ramadan, the ruling remains the same)."
"3491","I would see water dripping from his hair, but he would still fast that day. The narrator named Mutarrif says: I asked Imam Sha’bi: Did this happen in the month of Ramadan? He replied: In this matter, the month of Ramadan and other months have the same status."
"3492","The man said: You are not like us. Allah Almighty has forgiven your past and future sins. So the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: I hope that I am the most God-fearing among you and the most knowledgeable among you regarding what leads to piety. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): The statement of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), ""I hope,"" contains evidence that a person may verbally express hope regarding something about which he has no doubt. It also contains evidence that making an exception in an oath in this manner is permissible, as we have mentioned at the beginning of the book."
"3493","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would enter the state of major ritual impurity (janabah) due to marital relations and would reach the time of true dawn (subh sadiq) in that state, then he would fast. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): The narrator named Abdullah bin Abdur Rahman is Ma'mar bin Hazm Abu Tawalah, who belongs to the people of Madinah and is trustworthy."
"3494","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) would be in a state of major ritual impurity (janabah) at the time of true dawn due to marital relations, yet he would still observe the fast."
"3495","Messenger of Allah, (the time) of prayer overtakes me as I am in a state of junub; should I observe fast (in this state)? Upon this the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: (At times the time) of prayer overtakes me while I am in a state of junub, and I observe fast (in that very state), whereupon he said: Messenger of Allah, you are not like us Allah has pardoned all your sins, the previous ones and the later ones. Upon this he (the Holy Prophet) said: By Allah, I hope I am the most God-fearirg of you, and possess the best knowledge among you of those (things) against which I should guard. (Using translation from Muslim 1110)"
"3496","Lady Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) and Lady Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her), who are the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), narrate: Sometimes the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would be in a state of major ritual impurity (janabah) at the time of true dawn due to having been with his wife, but he would still perform ghusl (ritual bath) and observe the fast."
"3497","Lady Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) (sometimes) would be in a state of major ritual impurity (janabah) at the time of true dawn without having had a wet dream, but even then he would fast on that day."
"3498","narrated this. Sometimes, due to having relations with his wife, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would be in a state of major ritual impurity (janabah) at the time of true dawn, and then he would observe the fast."
"3499","I set out and we presented ourselves before Sayyidah Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) and Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), who are the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). We asked both of them about this matter, so both of them informed us that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would sometimes be in a state of major ritual impurity at the time of true dawn, but it was not due to a wet dream, then he would fast. (The narrator says) Then we went to Marwan bin Hakam and informed him about the statements of both women and the statement of Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), so Marwan said: I urge both of you to go to Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) and inform him about this matter. (The narrator says) Then we met Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him). He was at the door of the mosque at that time. We said to him: The governor has instructed us to mention this matter before you. He asked: What is it? So my father narrated the whole incident to him, upon which the color of Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah’s (may Allah be pleased with him) face changed and he said: Sayyiduna Fadl bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated the hadith to me in this way. In any case, they would know better. Imam Zuhri narrates: They had misunderstood the meaning of the hadith."
"3500","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be in a state of janabah at the time of true dawn, then he would fast. (The narrator says) So Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) rejected this person's statement."
"3501","The man said: You are not like us. Allah Almighty has forgiven your past and future sins. So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I hope that I am the most God-fearing among you and the most knowledgeable about what is piety."
"3502","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""The people will remain on the right path as long as they hasten the breaking of the fast."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1957)"
"3503","The Prophet ﷺ said: Religion will continue to prevail as long as people hasten to break the fast, because the Jews and the Christians delay doing so. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2353)"
"3504","I never saw the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performing the Maghrib prayer before breaking his fast, even if it was just with a sip of water (that he would break his fast)."
"3505","I never saw the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) performing the Maghrib prayer before breaking the fast, even if he took only a sip of water for iftar."
"3506","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""The people will remain on the right path as long as they hasten the breaking of the fast."" (Using translation from Bukhārī 1957)"
"3507","the Messenger of Allah said: ""Allah, Mighty and Sublime is He, said: 'Those of My worshippers who are most beloved to me are the quickest to break their fast.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 700)"
"3508","the Messenger of Allah said: ""Allah, Mighty and Sublime is He, said: 'Those of My worshippers who are most beloved to me are the quickest to break their fast.'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 700)"
"3509","The Prophet ﷺ said: Religion will continue to prevail as long as people hasten to break the fast, because the Jews and the Christians delay doing so. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 2353)"
"3510","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “My Ummah will remain upon my Sunnah as long as they do not wait for the stars (to appear) for breaking the fast.” The narrator states: When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was fasting, he would instruct someone to climb a high place and observe; when that person informed him that the sun had set, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) would break his fast."
"3511","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Dismount and mix sattu for us."" The narrator says: That companion dismounted. He mixed sattu for the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) drank it. Then he said: ""When you see night approaching from this side, then the fasting person should break his fast."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) meant that it comes from the east."
"3512","The sun has not (yet set). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Get down and mix sattu for us. The man got down and mixed the sattu, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drank it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you see that the night has come from this side and the day has departed from that side, then the fasting person should break his fast. In this narration, the word ""ajdih"" means to soak the sattu. This has been stated by Imam Abu Hatim."
"3513","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:“When night comes and day departs, and the sun sets, then (it is time to) break your fast.ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 231)"
"3514","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever finds dates should break his fast with them, and whoever does not find them should break his fast with water, for it is a means of purification."
"3515","""When any one of you breaks his fast, let him break it with dates. If he cannot find dates, then let him break it with water, for it is a means of purification."" (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 1699)"
"3516","If one amongst us had to break fasts (of Ramadan due to natural reasons, i. e. menses) during the life of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ she could not find it possible to complete them so long she had been in the presence of Messenger of Allah ﷺ till Sha'ban commenced. (Using translation from Muslim 1146e)"
"3517","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""You should fast another day in its place."
"3518","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever vomits unintentionally while fasting, there is no making up (qada) required for him, but whoever vomits deliberately must make up (qada) for it."
"3519","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this statement of the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him: \""When a fasting person forgetfully eats something or forgetfully drinks something, he should complete his fast, for it is Allah Almighty who has fed him and given him drink.\"""""
"3520","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a fasting person forgetfully eats something, he should complete his fast, f"
"3521","narrates this statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Whoever eats something forgetfully during the month of Ramadan, then making up (the fast) is not obligatory upon him, nor is expiation obligatory upon him."
"3522","I was fasting and then I ate and drank out of forgetfulness."" So the Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Allah Almighty has fed you and given you drink; complete your fast."
"3523","I am not able to do any of these. A basket of dates was brought to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He said: Take it and give it as charity. He said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! I do not find anyone more in need of it than myself. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) smiled until his molar teeth became visible. He said: Then eat it yourself. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:): In this narration, apart from Imam Malik and Ibn Jurayj, no other narrator from al-Zuhri has transmitted these words: ""or he should fast for two months, or feed sixty needy people."" The statement of this man that I have broken my fast means: I had intercourse (during the fast)."
